# Business rules

All Business / Domain service conventions live in this file. When adding a new business-related rule, append a section here — do not create a new `.mdc` file.

## No UI code in Business (hard rule)

- **Never** put Avalonia / WPF / WinForms / HTML / XAML, `Window`, `UserControl`, buttons, dialogs, brushes, or any presentation types in `CoperativeTelouet.Business` (or Domain).
- **Never** reference `CoperativeTelouet.UI` from Business.
- **Never** show message boxes or build UI from a business service — return results / throw `ValidationException`; the UI layer shows dialogs.
- Business may contain French validation **messages** (strings) — that is not UI chrome.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — UI inside Business
public class ClientService {
    public void Save(...) {
        MessageBox.Show("OK"); // or any Avalonia Window
    }
}

// ✅ GOOD — Business returns/throws; UI shows dialog
await _clients.CreateClientAsync(dto); // UI catches and calls IUserDialogService
```

## Layer separation

Layers: **UI → Business → DataAccess → Domain**. Dependencies point inward only. Put as much product logic as possible in Business so the UI stays replaceable.

| Layer | Owns | Does not own |
|-------|------|--------------|
| **Domain** | Entities, enums, pure rules | EF, DTOs, UI, services |
| **DataAccess** | DbContext, EF, migrations, repositories | Business rules, ViewModels |
| **Business** | Services, DTOs, validators, mapping, workflows | DbContext, EF LINQ, SQL, Avalonia |
| **UI** | Views, ViewModels, dialogs, binding | Direct DB access, business calculations |

- Never put pricing, stock, document numbering, or validation orchestration in ViewModels — call Business services.
- Prefer new features as Business methods (+ DTOs/validators) first; UI only binds and invokes.
- Business → `IRepository<>` + Domain; no Avalonia references.
- **UI must never call DataAccess** — only Business. `AddBusiness(connectionString)` registers DataAccess internally; expose startup via `IAppDatabaseInitializer`, not DataAccess types.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — business rule in ViewModel
if (etat == EtatBac.Plein && chambreId is null) { /* reject */ }

// ✅ GOOD — ViewModel calls Business
await _categorieService.CreateAsync(new CreateCategorieDto(Nom));
```

## GenericService (required pattern)

Specialized services must **inherit** `GenericService<TEntity, TDto, TCreateDto, TUpdateDto>` and reuse its CRUD.
Specialized service **interfaces** must **extend** `IGenericService<…>` and declare **only** domain-specific methods — never redeclare CRUD (`GetByIdAsync`, `CreateAsync`, `UpdateAsync`, …).

- **Do** declare `IClientService : IGenericService<Tiers, TiersDto, CreateTiersDto, UpdateTiersDto>` (same for fournisseur, …).
- **Do** call inherited CRUD from UI / other services: `CreateAsync`, `UpdateAsync`, `GetByIdAsync`, `FindAsync`.
- **Do** add custom methods only when they add domain behavior (`GetClientsAsync`, `ToggleActifAsync`, `GetCompteAsync`).
- **Don't** wrap CRUD in aliases (`CreateClientAsync`, `GetClientByIdAsync`, …) — that duplicates `IGenericService`.
- **Don't** mark any `GenericService` member `virtual` / `abstract` / `override` — never override the base.
- **Don't** reimplement CRUD, validators, or mapping beside GenericService.
- Simple catalog entities: closed `GenericService<…>` DI registration is enough (no subclass / no specialized interface).

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — only domain methods; CRUD comes from IGenericService
public interface IClientService : IGenericService<Tiers, TiersDto, CreateTiersDto, UpdateTiersDto>
{
    Task<IReadOnlyList<TiersDto>> GetClientsAsync(string? search = null, CancellationToken ct = default);
    Task<TiersDto> ToggleActifAsync(int id, CancellationToken ct = default);
}

// ❌ BAD — CRUD aliases that duplicate IGenericService
public interface IClientService : IGenericService<...>
{
    Task<TiersDto> CreateClientAsync(CreateTiersDto dto, ...);
    Task<TiersDto?> GetClientByIdAsync(int id, ...);
}

// ❌ BAD
public override async Task<TiersDto> CreateAsync(...) { ... }
```

## AutoMapper

- Use AutoMapper for DTO ↔ entity and DTO ↔ DTO — declare maps in `Mapping/*Profile.cs`.
- Prefer `Mapper.Map<T>(…)` over hand-copying properties.
- Use record `with { … }` after map when only one/few fields change.

```csharp
var update = Mapper.Map<UpdateTiersDto>(dto) with { Actif = !dto.Actif };
await UpdateAsync(id, update, ct);
```

## Filtered reads from Business

- Prefer `FindAsync(predicate)` (via GenericService or `Repo`) so SQL applies `WHERE`.
- Never `GetAllAsync()` then `.Where` in memory for large tables.

## FluentValidation / field rules

- One `AbstractValidator<T>` per Create/Update DTO; invoked from GenericService / services.
- **ICE (Tiers):** optional (empty/null allowed). If provided, exactly **15** characters.

**Rule of thumb:** GenericService for CRUD (never virtualize), custom methods for domain rules, AutoMapper for mapping, validators for input shape.
